        "Here is a classic example. Premise one: all humans are mortal. Premise two: Socrates is a human. Conclusion: Socrates is mortal. This pattern, called a syllogism, was studied in detail by Aristotle, who is often called the founder of formal logic. Centuries later, the philosopher al-Farabi wrote so much about Aristotle's logic that he became known in the Islamic world as the Second Teacher, Aristotle being the First.",
