        { q: "According to the Four Noble Truths, what is the origin of suffering?", options: ["The anger of the gods", "Bad luck", "Craving", "Karma from past lives alone"], answer: 2, why: "The second Noble Truth identifies craving as the cause of suffering." },
        { q: "What does the Daoist idea of wu wei mean?", options: ["Strict obedience to rituals", "Military discipline", "Total inactivity and laziness", "Effortless action in harmony with the natural flow of things"], answer: 3, why: "Wu wei is acting without forcing, like water flowing around obstacles." }
