        { q: "What was Locke's main argument in A Letter Concerning Toleration?", options: ["Kings should choose their subjects' religion", "Religion should be banned", "Government protects civil interests, while true faith cannot be forced", "Only Christians deserve freedom"], answer: 2, why: "Locke separated civil government from the care of souls." },
        { q: "Which statement presents an argument made by supporters of secularism?", options: ["Separation protects religion from state interference as well as the state from religion", "Faith should always be enforced by law", "A shared state religion gives a society moral direction", "Laws should never reflect any values"], answer: 0, why: "Secularists often argue separation benefits both religion and state." }
