        { q: "What did Nietzsche mean by 'God is dead'?", options: ["God literally died at a specific moment", "Belief in God had stopped being the foundation of European culture, with serious consequences", "Religion is good for society", "Everyone should become a madman"], answer: 1, why: "He was describing a cultural shift and warning about what would follow." },
        { q: "What is a 'steelman'?", options: ["The strongest version of your opponent's argument", "A weakened version of your opponent's argument", "An insult used in debates", "A type of logical fallacy"], answer: 0, why: "Steelmanning is the opposite of a straw man: engaging the best version of a view." }
